SEARCH ALL 'f': its OCCURS clause has no KEY phrase (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 1)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: each relation tests a KEY of the table (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN tests a later KEY without 'k1', which comes before it (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: the key 'k1' is subscripted by the table's first index 'i' at its level, without + or - (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: a key = a value, or a condition-name of one value, joined by AND; no OR, NOT or other relation (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: a key = a value, or a condition-name of one value, joined by AND; no OR, NOT or other relation (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: the value compared with 'k1' is neither a key of the table nor subscripted by 'i' (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL ... WHEN: the KEY data-name is written first, key = value (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 4)
SEARCH ALL has one WHEN (X3.23-1985 SEARCH format 2)
SEARCH with NEXT SENTENCE ends at the period, not END-SEARCH (X3.23-1985 SEARCH syntax rule 5)
